      "content": "Yes, the native character, as I've come to understand it. The Bengalis, in particular, can be a trying lot - mercurial, superstitious, and prone to gossip and malicious rumor. Their cultural norms are, I dare say, rather... romanticized in comparison to our own value system, which relies on clear boundaries, direct communication, and a no-nonsense approach to governance. I've observed, anecdotally, that the Bengalis' propensity for emotional reaction and revenge can be... satisfactory diffused by a firm application of British authority, tempered, of course, by benevolence and fairness. One must avoid appearing capricious or merely tyrannical, but a display of assertive leadership can be both calming and reassuring to our subjects.",
